  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Modern Technology Solutions has secured $444M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, from 50 awards with an average award size of $8.9M. Obligations rose up 12.3% year over year, continuing a multi-year trend that shows growth since FY21 when obligations were $137M. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, obligating $263M, followed by the Department of Defense with $174M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Biotechnology) is the largest market at $252M, with a related R&D category at $124M and Engineering Services at $42.2M. Modern Technology Solutions also works in smaller markets such as Custom Computer Programming Services at $7.4M and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $5.1M. Current-year totals are partial and cover fiscal year to date, so FY2026 figures represent obligations recorded so far in the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Modern Technology Solutions' federal business trended over recent years?",
        "body": "Modern Technology Solutions' federal obligations increased from $137M in FY21 to $444M in FY26. Obligations rose up 12.3% year over year into FY2026 to date, with a peak at $396M in FY25 before the current FY26 total of $444M. The company has grown both its award count and average award size, reflected in 50 awards averaging $8.9M in FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main government buyers and what services do they buy?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the top buyer, obligating $263M, followed by the Department of Defense with $174M and the Department of Homeland Security with $7M. Modern Technology Solutions' largest markets are R&D in the physical, engineering, and life sciences at $252M and a related R&D category at $124M, with Engineering Services at $42.2M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $7.4M."
      }
    ]
